{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Different Shades Of Blue felt like a natural next choice because blues guitar connects with what drew me to my recent Clapton and Hendrix listening.",
    "A Fool To Care appealed because my interest in Memphis makes another Boz Scaggs album a meaningful continuation; the roots-oriented and blues-rock choices also fit my current interests."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "25 missed my current interest because pop vocals do not offer the blues guitar and roots-rock sound I want today.",
    "Wallflower's mellow vocal emphasis felt less relevant to my current mood, while the live blues album interested me but was less compelling than trying a studio album first."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "My interest in some vocal-led albums seems to have been stretched into an interest in vocal albums generally, although the musical style matters much more to me.",
    "An album being broadly related to classic rock or familiar performers is not enough to make it an immediate choice; I am especially drawn to blues guitar right now."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "The direct connection between Memphis and another Boz Scaggs album matters more to me than a loose resemblance between albums.",
    "I rarely choose many albums at once: several blues recommendations appeal to me, but choosing two today does not mean I dislike the others."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations largely understood my interest in blues and roots rock, but some broadened that interest too far toward vocal albums and missed how selectively I act on good matches."
}"}
